ZeroClaw chord-reveal architecture plan

Project shape
- Vite + strict TypeScript client-only Minesweeper app.
- Core game behavior lives in pure modules under `src/game/`; DOM and input
  wiring stay in `src/ui/` and `src/input/`.
- Unit coverage uses Vitest under `tests/unit/`; browser coverage uses
  Playwright specs under `e2e/`.

Current module structure
- `src/game/engine.ts`: game state machine and public actions.
- `src/game/reveal.ts`: reveal flow and flood-fill behavior.
- `src/game/flag.ts`: flag/question-mark mark cycling.
- `src/game/board.ts` and `src/game/first-click.ts`: board helpers and
  first-click-safe mine placement.
- `src/input/pointer.ts`: unified pointer intent mapping for mouse/touch/pen.
- `src/input/long-press.ts`: long-press helper used by touch flagging.
- `src/ui/app.ts`: application controller that dispatches input intents into
  engine actions and updates the board/status/overlay.
- `src/ui/board-view.ts`, `src/ui/status-bar.ts`, `src/ui/controls.ts`, and
  `src/ui/outcome-overlay.ts`: focused DOM renderers.
- `src/types.ts`: shared game, cell, board, status, action, and input types.

Issue dependencies
- #57 is the foundation: add the `reveal-adjacent` engine action and chord
  algorithm. It should land before any UI wiring.
- #58 can be implemented independently after reading the existing pointer
  normalization path. It should emit a normalized `dblclick` cell intent
  without breaking long-press flagging.
- #59 depends on #57 and #58: route the new pointer intent through `src/ui/app.ts`
  only while the game is in `PLAYING`, then rely on the existing subscription
  update path.
- #60 depends on #59: add Playwright coverage for successful chord reveal,
  mismatched-flag no-op, and wrong-flag mine loss.

Key design decisions
- Keep chord behavior in `src/game/reveal.ts` or a small helper near reveal
  logic so the engine can stay a thin action/state coordinator.
- Chord no-ops when the target cell is unrevealed, has zero adjacency, or the
  count of flagged neighbors does not match the revealed number.
- When chord conditions pass, reveal every unflagged neighbor through the same
  reveal path used by normal cell reveal so flood-fill, win detection, and
  mine-hit loss remain consistent.
- Treat question-marked neighbors as unflagged for chord reveal unless the
  current mark model already defines otherwise.
- Extend shared action/input types in `src/types.ts` instead of stringly typed
  one-off plumbing.
- Add focused unit tests with deterministic boards before relying on E2E:
  engine/reveal tests for #57 and pointer tests for #58.
- Keep UI wiring minimal: `src/ui/app.ts` should dispatch the new action and
  reuse existing render/status updates rather than adding a separate UI path.
